       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like it might be a typo.\n\n**The problem:** For adults, amlodipine is usually 2.5\u201310 mg by mouth once daily, and **10 mg/day is the maximum**. 50 mg is five times that. An overdose of a calcium channel blocker can cause severe low blood pressure, slow heart rate and shock.\n\n**Did you mean 5 mg once daily?** That's a common starting dose, and \"5\" can easily become \"50\" when typing.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want:\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily\n- Something else. If 50 mg really is intended, please tell me the clinical reason so I can note it on the order.\n\nI'll enter it once you reply."
